# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and fill in your own key.
# ".env" is already in .gitignore - it will never be committed.
# NEVER put a real key in THIS file (.env.example) - it's tracked by git.

# Powers three things:
#   1. The final narration step on both the delay-recovery plan and the
#      budget trip plan (recovery_graph.py / trip_planner.py via llm_utils.py)
#   2. The sidebar chatbot's reasoning agent (chat_agent.py)
#   3. AI-suggested food spots/sightseeing for destinations with no curated
#      entry in intl_reference.py (always labeled "unverified" in the UI)
# Without these set, all three fall back to deterministic template text / a
# "not configured" message - the rest of the app still works fully.
#
# Pick ONE provider below and fill in that key - all of them are OpenAI-
# compatible under the hood, so no extra packages are needed for any option.
# Grok (xAI, x.ai) and Groq (groq.com) are two DIFFERENT companies with
# similar names - check your key's prefix if unsure ("xai-" vs "gsk_").

# --- Option A: OpenAI ---
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- Option B: Anthropic (Claude) ---
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# --- Option C: xAI (Grok) - keys start with "xai-", console.x.ai ---
# LLM_PROVIDER=grok
# GROK_API_KEY=xai-your-key-here
# GROK_MODEL=grok-4

# --- Option D: Groq (fast open-model hosting) - keys start with "gsk_", console.groq.com ---
LLM_PROVIDER=groq
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your-key-here
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# Flask session signing key - set this to any random string for real use.
SECRET_KEY=change-me-to-a-random-string

# Comma-separated list of emails that get admin access on signup/login.
ADMIN_EMAILS=aihemaharini@gmail.com

# --- Geoapify Places + Routing APIs (src/sightseeing.py, src/maps.py) ---
# Free account at myprojects.geoapify.com (3,000 requests/day free tier).
# Powers REAL sightseeing points-of-interest for destinations with no
# curated entry in intl_reference.py - tried before the LLM-guess fallback -
# AND the real airport-to-destination driving distance/time shown in the
# budget trip planner (maps.route_airport_to_place). Without this set,
# sightseeing falls through to curated data / LLM guess / generic template,
# and the airport transfer line is simply omitted - nothing crashes.
GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=your-geoapify-api-key

# --- Foursquare Places API (src/places.py) ---
# Free key at foursquare.com/developers - powers REAL named hotels with real
# street addresses and coordinates, replacing the LLM's "AI-suggested,
# unverified" property names. Ratings and prices are Premium fields that
# return HTTP 429 on the free tier, so this never supplies review data.
# Without this set, hotels fall back to the AI-suggested names as before.
FOURSQUARE_API_KEY=your-foursquare-api-key

# --- OpenSky Network (src/opensky.py) ---
# Free account at opensky-network.org, then create an API client - it issues a
# credentials.json holding clientId/clientSecret. Powers the live aircraft
# check: finds the real aircraft due to operate a flight, sees where it has
# been today, and how much ground time is left before the scheduled push.
# That fills prev_leg_arrival_delay, the model's strongest feature, which the
# form otherwise cannot supply. Without it, predictions fall back to schedule
# and weather only - nothing breaks.
OPENSKY_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id
OPENSKY_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret

# --- AviationStack (src/aviationstack.py) ---
# Free key at aviationstack.com. The ONLY source here that knows a flight's
# delay BEFORE it departs: it publishes the airline schedule and an estimated
# departure against it, so a flight that has not moved yet already carries a
# delay figure. OpenSky cannot do this - it reports aircraft that have already
# flown - so without this the model runs with prev_leg_known=0 on every live
# prediction. Also supplies real future timetables (flightsFuture), replacing
# generated flight numbers in the trip catalogue.
# The free plan allows roughly 100 calls a MONTH, so responses are cached on
# disk and a hard cap refuses calls past AVIATIONSTACK_MONTHLY_CAP, leaving the
# app to fall back to schedule+weather rather than fail. Historical flight_date,
# airlines and routes are NOT on the free plan.
AVIATIONSTACK_API_KEY=your-aviationstack-key
AVIATIONSTACK_MONTHLY_CAP=90

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live flight search (Delay Check -> "Live Flights")
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Aviationstack: real-time flights. Free plan = ~100 calls/MONTH, so every search is cached.
# AVIATIONSTACK_API_KEY=your_key_here
# AVIATIONSTACK_MONTHLY_CAP=90
# FLIGHT_SEARCH_CACHE_TTL_S=300   # reuse an identical live search for this many seconds
#
# Weather for the delay model comes from Open-Meteo, which needs NO key.
# WeatherAPI.com is a separate optional live-conditions source:
# WEATHERAPI_KEY=your_key_here
#
# Optional fares in flight details (Google Flights via SerpApi):
# SERPAPI_KEY=your_key_here
#
# SECRET_KEY=change-me   # Flask session signing key; set a long random value in production
